Resolve a fixed subject census into identity groups only.

Do not decide ontology type, page maturity, containment, or claim ownership. Every supplied node must occur in
exactly one identity group. Merge nodes into one group only when the evidence affirmatively establishes the same
continuing real-world subject. This explicit grouping is authoritative downstream: never emit competing groups for
the same identity.

Resolve a group to an existing exact registry ID only with stable-name, explicit alias or rename, or defining-history
evidence. Shared vocabulary, participants, apparent type, or being the only registry option is insufficient. Use
review_required when the evidence cannot distinguish an existing identity from a new one; list every materially
plausible existing candidate. Otherwise declare a new identity. Preserve a source-grounded preferred title and
aliases, explain the identity evidence, and return JSON matching the schema.
